{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-pro-28-1","title":"Proverbs 28:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 General observations of impiety and religious integrity.</p>\n<p>wicked. Le 26:17,36; De 28:7,25; 2Ki 7:6,7,15; Ps 53:5; Isa 7:2; Jer 20:4 the righteous. Ex 11:8; Ps 27:1,2; 46:2,3; 112:7; Isa 26:3,4; Da 3:16-18; 6:10,11 Ac 4:13; 14:3; 1Th 2:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-2","title":"Proverbs 28:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the transgression. 1Ki 15:25,28; 16:8-29; 2Ki 15:8-31; 2Ch 36:1-12; Isa 3:1-7 Ho 13:11 but. Ge 45:5-8; 2Ch 32:20-26; Job 22:28-30; Ec 9:15; Isa 58:12; Da 4:27 by a man, etc. by men of understanding and wisdom shall theylikewise be prolonged.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-3","title":"Proverbs 28:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>poor man. Mt 18:28-30 which leaveth no food. Heb. without food.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-4","title":"Proverbs 28:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>that. 1Sa 23:19-21; Ps 10:3; 49:18; Jer 5:30; Mt 3:15; Ac 12:22; 24:2-4 Ro 1:32; 1Jo 4:5 but. 1Sa 15:14-24; 22:14,15; 1Ki 18:18,21; 20:41,42; 21:19,20; 22:19-28 2Ki 3:13,14; Ne 5:7-13; 13:8-11,17-20,23-26,28; Mt 3:7; 14:4 Ac 15:2; 19:9; Ga 2:3-6; Eph 5:11; 1Th 2:2; Jude 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-5","title":"Proverbs 28:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>15:24; 24:7; Ps 25:14; 92:6; Jer 4:22; Mr 4:10-13; Joh 7:17 1Co 2:14,15; Jas 1:5; 1Jo 2:20,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-6","title":"Proverbs 28:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>18; 16:8; 19:1,22; Lu 16:19-23; Ac 24:24-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-7","title":"Proverbs 28:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>keepeth. 2:1-6; 3:1-35 but. 24; 19:26; 23:19-22; 29:3,15; Lu 15:13,30; 1Pe 4:3,4 is a companion of riotous men. or, feedeth gluttons.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-8","title":"Proverbs 28:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>that by. 13:22; Job 27:16,17; Ec 2:26 unjust gain. Heb. by increase. Le 25:36; Eze 18:8,13,17 pity. 19:7; 2Sa 12:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-9","title":"Proverbs 28:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>turneth. 21:13; Isa 1:15,16; 58:7-11; Zec 7:11-13; 2Ti 4:3,4 even. 15:8; Ps 66:18; 109:7; Lu 13:25-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-10","title":"Proverbs 28:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>causeth. Nu 31:15,16; 1Sa 26:19; Ac 13:8-10; Ro 16:17,18; 2Co 11:3,4,13-15 Ga 1:8,9; 2:4; 3:1-4; 2Pe 2:18-20; Re 2:14 he shall. 26:27; Ps 7:15,16; 9:15; Ec 10:8 but. 10:3; 15:6; 21:20; De 7:12-14; Ps 37:11,25,26; Mt 6:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-11","title":"Proverbs 28:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>rich. 18:11; 23:4; Isa 10:13,14; Eze 28:3-5; Lu 16:13,14; 1Co 3:18,19 1Ti 6:17 his own conceit. Heb. his eyes. 26:16; Isa 5:21; Ro 11:25; 12:16 the poor. 18:17; 19:1; Job 32:9; Ec 9:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-12","title":"Proverbs 28:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>righteous. 28; 11:10; 29:2; 1Ch 15:25-28; 16:7-36; 29:20-22; 2Ch 7:10; 30:22-27 Es 8:15-17; Job 29:11-20; Lu 19:37,38 but. 1Sa 24:11; 1Ki 17:3-24; 18:13; 19:3; Ec 10:6,16; Jer 36:26 Heb 11:37,38 hidden. Heb. sought for. Jer 5:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-13","title":"Proverbs 28:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>that. 10:12; 17:9; Ge 3:12,13; 4:9; 1Sa 15:13,24; Job 31:33; Ps 32:3-5 Jer 2:22,23; Mt 23:25-28 whoso. Le 26:40-42; 1Ki 8:47-49; Job 33:27; Ps 51:1-5,10; Jer 3:12,13 Da 9:20-23; Lu 15:18-24; 1Jo 1:8-10 and forsaketh. Ex 10:16,17; 1Sa 15:30; Mt 3:6-10; 27:4,5; Ac 26:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-14","title":"Proverbs 28:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Happy. 23:17; Ps 2:11; 16:8; 112:1; Isa 66:2; Jer 32:40; Ro 11:20; Heb 4:1 1Pe 1:17 but. 29:1; Ex 7:22; 14:23; Job 9:4; Ro 2:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-15","title":"Proverbs 28:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>a roaring. 20:2; Ho 5:11; 1Pe 5:8 a ranging. 17:12; 2Ki 2:24; Ho 13:8 so. Ex 1:14-16,22; 1Sa 22:17-19; 2Ki 15:16; 21:16; Es 3:6-10; Mt 2:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-16","title":"Proverbs 28:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>prince. 1Ki 12:10,14; Ne 5:15; Ec 4:1; Isa 3:12; Am 4:1 he that. Ex 18:21; Isa 33:15,16; Jer 22:15-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-17","title":"Proverbs 28:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Ge 9:6; Ex 21:14; Nu 35:14-34; 1Ki 21:19,23; 2Ki 9:26 2Ch 24:21-25; Mt 27:4,5; Ac 28:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-18","title":"Proverbs 28:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>walketh. 10:9,25; 11:3-6; Ps 25:21; 26:11; 84:11; Ga 2:14 but. 6; Nu 22:32; Ps 73:18-20; 125:5; 1Th 5:3; 2Pe 2:1-3; Re 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-19","title":"Proverbs 28:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>that tilleth. 12:11; 14:4; 27:23-27 but. 13:20; 23:20,21; Jud 9:4; Lu 15:12-17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-20","title":"Proverbs 28:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>faithful. 20:6; 1Sa 22:14; Ne 7:2; Ps 101:6; 112:4-9; Lu 12:42; 16:1,10-12 1Co 4:2-5; Re 2:10,13 but. 22; 13:11; 20:21; 23:4; 2Ki 5:20-27; 1Ti 6:9,10 innocent. or, unpunished. 17:5; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-21","title":"Proverbs 28:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>respect. 18:5; 24:23; Ex 23:2,8 for.Erasmus observes that this expression probably originated from the circumstance of holding out a piece of bread to a dog, in order to soothe him.</p>\n<p>Eze 13:19; Ho 4:18; Mic 3:5; 7:3; Ro 16:18; 2Pe 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-22","title":"Proverbs 28:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>that hasteth, etc. Heb. that hath an evil eye, hasteth to berich. 20; 1Ti 6:9 an evil. 23:6; Mt 20:15; Mr 7:22 and. Ge 13:10-13; 19:17; Job 20:18-22; 27:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-23","title":"Proverbs 28:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>27:5,6; 2Sa 12:7; 1Ki 1:23,32-40; Ps 141:5; Mt 18:15; Ga 2:11 2Pe 3:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-24","title":"Proverbs 28:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>robbeth. 19:26; Jud 17:2; Mt 15:4-6 the same. 7; 13:20; 18:9 a destroyer. Heb. a man destroying.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-25","title":"Proverbs 28:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>that is. 10:12; 13:10; 15:18; 21:24; 22:10; 29:22 he that putteth. Ps 84:12; Jer 17:7,8; 1Ti 6:6 made. 11:25; 13:4; 15:30; Isa 58:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-26","title":"Proverbs 28:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>that. 3:5; 2Ki 8:13; Jer 17:9; Mr 7:21-23; 14:27-31; Ro 8:7 but. Job 28:28; 2Ti 3:15; Jas 1:5; 3:13-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-27","title":"Proverbs 28:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>that giveth. 19:17; 22:9; De 15:7,10; Ps 41:1-3; 112:5-9; 2Co 9:6-11; Heb 13:16 hideth. Isa 1:15 shall. 11:26; 24:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-28-28","title":"Proverbs 28:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>the wicked. 12; 29:2 hide. Job 24:4 they perish. Es 8:17; Ac 12:23,24</p>"}]}